<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolás Salmerón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1838">1838</a>–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolás Salmerón (1838–1908) was a Spanish philosopher and republican politician who served as president of the executive power of the First Spanish Republic from July to September 1873. He suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantonal-rebellion">Cantonal Rebellion</a> but resigned rather than sign death sentences for soldiers. A professor at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, he remained a leader of Spanish republicanism and later headed the Solidaridad Catalana coalition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-salmeron.jpg" alt="Nicolás Salmerón" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico de Madrazo y Kuntz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F._de_Madrazo_-_1879,_Nicol%C3%A1s_Salmer%C3%B3n_(Congreso_de_los_Diputados,_Madrid,_131_x_96_cm).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
